   "id": "avodah_zarah.29a.13",
   "daf": "29a",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "וְגוֹי הַמִּסְתַּפֵּר מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל, כֵּיוָן שֶׁהִגִּיעַ לִבְלוֹרִיתוֹ שׁוֹמֵט אֶת יָדוֹ. וְכַמָּה? אָמַר רַב מַלְכִּיָּה אָמַר רַב אַדָּא בַּר אַהֲבָה: שָׁלֹש אֶצְבָּעוֹת לְכׇל רוּחַ וָרוּחַ.",
   "en": "The baraita stated: «And» in the case of «a gentile who has his hair cut by a Jew, when» the Jew «reaches» the gentile’s «forelock, he removes his hand» and does not cut it, because it is associated with idol worship. The Gemara asks: «And how much» space should the Jew leave around the forelock? «Rav Malkiyya says» that «Rav Adda bar Ahava says: Three fingerbreadths in each and every direction.»"
  }
